35,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems that how we structure our days and the environment we're in really impact our group dynamic. Last year, some of us barely saw each other between meals, which felt like a missed opportunity.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It's so important that we spend quality time together. I found that renting a whole house on the islands is quite affordable, but we should think carefully about how we handle the meal costs.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that the inns have very strict times for meals and baths. Also, some houses only have one bathroom for everyone, and the water might get cold. That sounds a bit scary.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I noticed that the ferry schedule is quite restrictive, which means we'd lose two full days just to travel. On the other hand, a city location would be much more flexible for getting around.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I noticed that city beds can be quite expensive and vary a lot in price. Also, last time we booked separately, the costs were uneven across the group, which felt a bit unfair.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Jonathan, if the ferry takes two days, that's a lot of time spent in transit. @Minato, the bathroom situation sounds stressful; we shouldn't let basic logistics ruin the mood of the trip.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, it's a shame that the costs felt uneven last time. I think we should look for a way to make the payments simple and fair for everyone, so no one feels burdened.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,I agree with Mizuki. I'm a little worried about the cold water and the strict schedules. I wonder if there is a place where we can just relax and not have to rush?,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Minato. A place where we aren't tied to a strict clock or a rigid ferry schedule would be much more peaceful. Flexibility allows us to actually enjoy the destination.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, I completely agree. I'd feel much more relaxed if we had a single, clear cost for the whole stay rather than dealing with different prices for each room. It would be so much simpler.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"If we want to avoid feeling either too crowded or too disconnected, we need a place that allows for both shared activities and a bit of personal space. A town setting might be the best compromise.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"A town setting could be lovely, but I worry that if we buy meals separately, some of us might feel pressured to spend more than they can afford just to keep up.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I think having our own rooms might be nice too. If we are all in one room on futons, I wonder if it will be hard to find a quiet place to sit when we aren't sleeping?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"That is a valid concern, Minato. I also feel that having a bit of quiet space is essential. If we choose a location with easy transport, we can spend less time waiting and more time relaxing.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree that having some quiet space is important. However, I'm still worried about the budget. If we go with a town setting and separate rooms, won't the final costs be unpredictable for everyone?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,We can manage the budget by setting a clear cap or choosing a mid-range hotel. The priority should be a location that naturally encourages us to stay together without feeling trapped.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree, Mizuki. Perhaps a place with a fixed all-in rate would be the kindest way to ensure no one is quietly struggling with the costs while we are trying to enjoy ourselves.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I think a place with a fixed price sounds very safe. I just hope we can find somewhere that isn't too strict with the times, so we can all be happy and relaxed.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I think we should prioritize a destination that minimizes the time spent on logistics. If we avoid restrictive schedules and long transit days, we can return home feeling truly refreshed rather than exhausted.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I think we're all agreeing that simplicity and fairness are key. A fixed, all-in rate for a whole building would be the most comforting option, as it removes the stress of unpredictable costs and uneven bills.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
