60,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Looking at the options, Option A seems the most balanced. It provides a shared base for meals and bonding, but the town setting allows us to step away for a bit of personal space when needed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option A sounds very lovely and peaceful. I like that the meals are included at the inn, as it takes away the worry of who is paying for what during our dinner conversations.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I'm a bit worried about Option A because of the strict meal times I found. But Option B's one bathroom and cold water sound scary, and Option C might be too lonely. Which one is the most relaxing?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Option A seems the most serene. It avoids the long transit days of the island trip and the chaotic planning of the city, allowing us to actually settle in and find some peace.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Shizue. Option A's included meals make the budget much more predictable. Option C sounds far too uncertain with separate bookings, and Option B's logistics seem a bit too stressful for a relaxing trip.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Minato, while the meal times are set, the town itself gives us the freedom to wander. It prevents the isolation of Option C and the claustrophobia of Option B. It's the safest bet for our group harmony.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minato, I understand your worry about the schedules, dear. But perhaps the structure will actually help us relax, knowing exactly when we'll be together. It feels like a very gentle way to travel.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I see. If the town is nice to walk in, maybe that's okay. But I'm still a little worried about sleeping in one room with everyone. Do you think we can find a quiet spot to sit?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, in a spa town, there are usually quiet cafes or parks where you can find a peaceful corner. It would be much more relaxing than the long ferry waits of Option B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Minato, I'm sure we can find a cozy cafe together! Also, Option A's fixed rates mean we won't have any surprises with the bill, which makes it much easier for everyone to truly relax.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Exactly. Option A provides the structure we need to ensure we actually spend time together, while the town environment prevents us from feeling trapped. It solves the issues of both isolation and overcrowding.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree completely. It feels like the most considerate choice for everyone. By having the meals and stay bundled together, we can focus on our friendship rather than the mathematics of the bill.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think you're all right. If we can find a quiet cafe and the town is peaceful, I'll feel better. I'll try my best to be okay with the meal times if it makes everyone happy.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we have found a common ground. Option A minimizes the logistical burden and the time spent in transit, which is the most important thing for me to ensure we return home feeling rested.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm so glad we've found a solution that makes everyone feel comfortable. Option A is the most balanced choice, ensuring we stay together while keeping the costs clear and fair for everyone from the start.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I'm glad we've reached a consensus. Option A respects our need for togetherness without sacrificing our individual peace of mind. I'm voting for Option A.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I feel very happy that we have all found a way to be comfortable. I will also vote for Option A, as it is the most gentle and fair for everyone.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'll vote for Option A too. Thank you for being so kind and helping me feel better about it. I'm looking forward to finding a quiet cafe with you all!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Option A is the most efficient and peaceful choice, allowing us to maximize our rest and minimize the stress of travel. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I'm so happy we're all on the same page! Option A is perfect because it's fair, predictable, and peaceful for everyone. I'll vote for Option A as well.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
